 "ranking_deviation": "The contest selection ranks firms by rank(ROE) + rank(earnings yield). An earnings yield requires a share count. No point-in-time share counts exist in the data, and the 2026 snapshot covers only 300 of 3,649 listed firms -- a set that was itself chosen by the 2026 scoring pipeline, so screening on it would inject selection look-ahead into the as-of pool. The L1 ranking therefore uses the quality leg only, rank(ROE), with rank(ROE)+rank(operating margin) as a robustness check. This is a deviation from the contest formula: L1 validates the quality gate and the quality ranking, not the valuation leg. Disclosed in the Limitations section.",
